cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this dataset or code, please cite it using these metadata.
title: GPR161 deep mutational scan
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Data, processing pipeline and figure code for a saturation mutagenesis study of human
  GPR161. A library of 11,043 designed variants - missense, synonymous and
  single-residue deletions across 528 positions - was read out in three parallel FACS
  assays (cell-surface expression, whole-cell abundance, basal cAMP signalling) in
  HEK293T cells. The library was built for this study with the DIMPLE method, reads were
  processed with the Dumpling pipeline, and variant effects were estimated from the FACS
  bin counts with Lilace; the data is original to the accompanying paper. The repository
  holds the per-sample counts, the per-assay score tables, the pipeline that builds the
  variant and position tables from them, and the code for the figure panels.
